IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa28-part46`

-- coa28-part44.l4: Part 44 (Miscellaneous provisions), ss 1274-1283 of the Companies Act 2006,
-- lines 18349-18504 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (a plain-text rendering from legislation.gov.uk; not the official text).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Most of Part 44 amends other Acts. The words an amendment inserts are the law of the
-- Act they are inserted into; where they decide something about a person (a definition, a priority, a disclosure
-- rule, a bar on use) they are encoded here as functions; the amending instructions themselves, and the powers to
-- make regulations and rules that the amendments insert or this Part gives, are machinery and are not encoded
-- (inert, reason 2 in the coverage table of NOTES.md).
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN unless a comment says otherwise: JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words
-- (FALSE-kind comments), NOTHING otherwise (NOTHING-kind comments). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1274: Grants to bodies concerned with actuarial standards etc
-- (the definitions inserted into section 16(5) of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004)
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 1274(3) body` IS ONE OF
    `s 1274(3)(a) the Institute of Actuaries`
    `s 1274(3)(b) the Faculty of Actuaries in Scotland`
    `s 1274(3) another body`

-- src:18364 | “professional actuarial body” means—
-- src:18365 | (a) the Institute of Actuaries, or
-- src:18366 | (b) the Faculty of Actuaries in Scotland,
@ref s 1274(3) professional actuarial body (src:18364-18366)
GIVEN body IS A `s 1274(3) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1274(3) the body is a professional actuarial body` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `s 1274(3) another body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“professional actuarial body” means— (a) the Institute of Actuaries, or (b) the Faculty of Actuaries in Scotland"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:18367 | and the “members” of a professional actuarial body include persons who, although not members of the body, are subject to its rules in performing actuarial functions;
@ref s 1274(3) members of a professional actuarial body (src:18367)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, although not a member of the body, is subject to its rules in performing actuarial functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1274(3) the person is a member of a professional actuarial body` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the body` OR `the person, although not a member of the body, is subject to its rules in performing actuarial functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the “members” of a professional actuarial body include persons who, although not members of the body, are subject to its rules in performing actuarial functions"

DECLARE `s 1274(3) function` IS ONE OF
    `s 1274(3)(a) investigatory or disciplinary functions exercised by such bodies in relation to the performance by their members of actuarial functions`
    `s 1274(3)(b) the setting by such bodies of standards in relation to the performance by their members of actuarial functions`
    `s 1274(3)(c) the determining by such bodies of requirements in relation to the education and training of their members`
    `s 1274(3) another function`

-- src:18368 | “regulatory functions”, in relation to professional actuarial bodies, means any of the following—
-- src:18369 | (a) investigatory or disciplinary functions exercised by such bodies in relation to the performance by their members of actuarial functions,
-- src:18370 | (b) the setting by such bodies of standards in relation to the performance by their members of actuarial functions, and
-- src:18371 | (c) the determining by such bodies of requirements in relation to the education and training of their members;.
@ref s 1274(3) regulatory functions (src:18368-18371)
GIVEN function IS A `s 1274(3) function`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1274(3) the function is a regulatory function in relation to professional actuarial bodies` MEANS
    CONSIDER function
    WHEN `s 1274(3) another function` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“regulatory functions”, in relation to professional actuarial bodies, means any of the following— (a) ..., (b) ..., and (c) ..."
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1275: Levy to pay expenses of bodies concerned with actuarial standards etc
-- =========================================================================================================

-- The persons inserted as section 17(3A) of the 2004 Act: persons who may be required to pay the levy.
-- src:18376 | (3A) The following persons are within this subsection—
-- src:18377 | (a) the administrators of a public service pension scheme (within the meaning of section 1 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993);
-- src:18378 | (b) the trustees or managers of an occupational or personal pension scheme (within the meaning of that section)..
@ref s 1275(3) subsection (3A) persons (src:18376-18378)
GIVEN `the person is an administrator of a public service pension scheme (within the meaning of section 1 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a trustee or manager of an occupational or personal pension scheme (within the meaning of that section)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1275(3) the person is within subsection (3A) of section 17 of the 2004 Act` MEANS
    IF `the person is an administrator of a public service pension scheme (within the meaning of section 1 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993)` OR `the person is a trustee or manager of an occupational or personal pension scheme (within the meaning of that section)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following persons are within this subsection" (a) and (b), with no "only"

-- The words inserted as section 17(13): a draft that would be a hybrid instrument proceeds as if it were not.
-- src:18382 | (13) If a draft of any regulations to which subsection (10) applies would, apart from this subsection, be treated for the purposes of the standing orders of either House of Parliament as a hybrid instrument, it is to proceed in that House as if it were not such an instrument..
@ref s 1275(5) hybrid instruments (src:18382)
GIVEN `the draft is of regulations to which subsection (10) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the draft would, apart from this subsection, be treated for the purposes of the standing orders of either House of Parliament as a hybrid instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1275(5) the draft is to proceed in that House as if it were not a hybrid instrument` MEANS
    IF `the draft is of regulations to which subsection (10) applies` AND `the draft would, apart from this subsection, be treated for the purposes of the standing orders of either House of Parliament as a hybrid instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a draft of any regulations to which subsection (10) applies would, apart from this subsection, be treated ... as a hybrid instrument, it is to proceed in that House as if it were not such an instrument" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:18383 | (6) The above amendments have effect in relation to any exercise of the power to make regulations under section 17 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 after this section comes into force, regardless of when the expenses to be met by the levy in respect of which the regulations are made were incurred.
@ref s 1275(6) the time from which the amendments have effect (src:18383)
GIVEN `the regulations are made, in the exercise of the power under section 17 of the 2004 Act, after section 1275 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1275(6) the amendments have effect in relation to the exercise of the power`  MEANS
    IF `the regulations are made, in the exercise of the power under section 17 of the 2004 Act, after section 1275 comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "regardless of when the expenses to be met by the levy in respect of which the regulations are made were incurred"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to any exercise of the power ... after this section comes into force"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1276: Application of provisions to Scotland and Northern Ireland
-- =========================================================================================================

-- The words substituted as section 16(6) of the 2004 Act.
-- src:18389 | (6) In their application to Scotland, subsection (2)(a) to (t) are to be read as referring only to matters provision relating to which would be outside the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament..
@ref s 1276(2) application to Scotland (src:18389)
GIVEN `provision relating to the matter would be outside the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1276(2) the matter is one to which subsection (2)(a) to (t) of section 16 of the 2004 Act is read as referring in Scotland` MEANS
    IF `provision relating to the matter would be outside the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In their application to Scotland, subsection (2)(a) to (t) are to be read as referring only to matters provision relating to which would be outside the legislative competence of the Scottish Parliament"

-- src:18394 | (c) after that definition insert—
-- src:18395 | “the 1986 Order” means the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6))..
@ref s 1276(4)(c) the 1986 Order (src:18394-18395)
GIVEN `the instrument is the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6))` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1276(4)(c) the instrument is the 1986 Order` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6))`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the 1986 Order” means the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6))"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- ss 1277 to 1280: Information as to exercise of voting rights by institutional investors
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18404 | (3) In this section and the sections mentioned above—
-- src:18405 | (a) references to a person acting on behalf of an institution include—
-- src:18406 | (i) any person to whom authority has been delegated by the institution to take decisions as to any matter relevant to the subject matter of the regulations, and
-- src:18407 | (ii) such other persons as may be specified; and
@ref s 1277(3)(a) persons acting on behalf of an institution (src:18404-18407)
GIVEN `the person has been delegated authority by the institution to take decisions as to any matter relevant to the subject matter of the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is specified in the regulations as such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1277(3)(a) the person is a person acting on behalf of the institution` MEANS
    IF `the person has been delegated authority by the institution to take decisions as to any matter relevant to the subject matter of the regulations` OR `the person is specified in the regulations as such a person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to a person acting on behalf of an institution include"

-- src:18408 | (b) “specified” means specified in the regulations.
@ref s 1277(3)(b) "specified" (src:18408)
GIVEN `it is specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1277(3)(b) the matter is specified for the purposes of sections 1277 to 1280` MEANS
    IF `it is specified in the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified” means specified in the regulations"

-- src:18409 | (4) The obligation imposed by regulations under this section is enforceable by civil proceedings brought by—
-- src:18410 | (a) any person to whom the information should have been provided, or
-- src:18411 | (b) a specified regulatory authority.
@ref s 1277(4) enforcement of the obligation (src:18409-18411)
GIVEN `the obligation is imposed by regulations under section 1277` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person to whom the information should have been provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a specified regulatory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1277(4) the person may bring civil proceedings to enforce the obligation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the obligation is imposed by regulations under section 1277`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The obligation imposed by regulations under this section"
        IF `the person is a person to whom the information should have been provided` OR `the person is a specified regulatory authority`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "is enforceable by civil proceedings brought by— (a) ... or (b) ...", with no "only"

-- src:18413 | (6) Regulations under this section are subject to affirmative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1277(6) procedure (src:18413)
GIVETH A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
`s 1277(6) the procedure for regulations under section 1277` MEANS `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure`

-- ---- s 1278 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18415 | (1) The institutions to which section 1277 applies are—
-- src:18416 | (a) unit trust schemes within the meaning of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) in respect of which an order is in force under section 243 of that Act;
-- src:18417 | (b) open-ended investment companies incorporated by virtue of regulations under section 262 of that Act;
-- src:18418 | (c) companies approved for the purposes of Chapter 4 of Part 24 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010(investment trusts);
-- src:18419 | (d) pension schemes as defined in section 1(5) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (c. 48) or the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993 (c. 49);
-- src:18420 | (e) undertakings authorised under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on long-term insurance business (that is, the activity of effecting or carrying out contracts of long-term insurance within the meaning of the Financial Services and Markets (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 (S.I. 2001/544);
@ref s 1278(1) institutions to which section 1277 applies (src:18415-18420)
GIVEN `the institution is a unit trust scheme within the meaning of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 in respect of which an order is in force under section 243 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is an open-ended investment company incorporated by virtue of regulations under section 262 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is a company approved for the purposes of Chapter 4 of Part 24 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010 (investment trusts)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is a pension scheme as defined in section 1(5) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 or the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution is an undertaking authorised under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on long-term insurance business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1278(1) the institution is one to which section 1277 applies` MEANS
    IF       `the institution is a unit trust scheme within the meaning of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 in respect of which an order is in force under section 243 of that Act`
         OR  `the institution is an open-ended investment company incorporated by virtue of regulations under section 262 of that Act`
         OR  `the institution is a company approved for the purposes of Chapter 4 of Part 24 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010 (investment trusts)`
         OR  `the institution is a pension scheme as defined in section 1(5) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 or the Pension Schemes (Northern Ireland) Act 1993`
         OR  `the institution is an undertaking authorised under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to carry on long-term insurance business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The institutions to which section 1277 applies are— (a) ... (e)" with no "only", and sub-section (2)(a) lets regulations add others (points outside the text)

-- src:18425 | (3) The regulations must specify by whom, in the case of any description of institution, the duty imposed by the regulations is to be fulfilled.
@ref s 1278(3) who must fulfil the duty (src:18425)
GIVEN `the regulations specify, in the case of the description of institution, by whom the duty imposed by the regulations is to be fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1278(3) the regulations meet the requirement to specify by whom the duty is to be fulfilled` MEANS
    IF `the regulations specify, in the case of the description of institution, by whom the duty imposed by the regulations is to be fulfilled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The regulations must specify by whom, in the case of any description of institution, the duty imposed by the regulations is to be fulfilled" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- ---- s 1279 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18431 | (2) For this purpose an institution has an interest in shares if the shares, or a depositary certificate in respect of them, are held by it, or on its behalf.
@ref s 1279(2) interest in shares (src:18431)
GIVEN `the shares, or a depositary certificate in respect of them, are held by it, or on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1279(2) the institution has an interest in the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares, or a depositary certificate in respect of them, are held by it, or on its behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For this purpose an institution has an interest in shares if the shares, or a depositary certificate in respect of them, are held by it, or on its behalf" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18432 | A “depositary certificate” means an instrument conferring rights (other than options)—
-- src:18433 | (a) in respect of shares held by another person, and
-- src:18434 | (b) the transfer of which may be effected without the consent of that person.
@ref s 1279(2) depositary certificate (src:18432-18434)
GIVEN `it is an instrument conferring rights (other than options)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are in respect of shares held by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer of the instrument may be effected without the consent of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1279(2) the instrument is a depositary certificate` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument conferring rights (other than options)` AND `the rights are in respect of shares held by another person` AND `the transfer of the instrument may be effected without the consent of that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “depositary certificate” means an instrument conferring rights (other than options)— (a) in respect of shares held by another person, and (b) the transfer of which may be effected without the consent of that person"

-- src:18439 | (4) For this purpose a scheme or vehicle is taken to have an interest in shares if it would be regarded as having such an interest in accordance with subsection (2) if it was an institution to which section 1277 applied.
@ref s 1279(4) interest of a scheme or vehicle (src:18439)
GIVEN `the scheme or vehicle would be regarded as having an interest in the shares in accordance with subsection (2) if it were an institution to which section 1277 applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1279(4) the scheme or vehicle is taken to have an interest in the shares` MEANS
    IF `the scheme or vehicle would be regarded as having an interest in the shares in accordance with subsection (2) if it were an institution to which section 1277 applied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a scheme or vehicle is taken to have an interest in shares if it would be regarded as having such an interest in accordance with subsection (2) if it was an institution to which section 1277 applied" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18435 | (3) Where an institution has an interest—
-- src:18436 | (a) in a specified description of collective investment scheme (within the meaning of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8)), or
-- src:18437 | (b) in any other specified description of scheme or collective investment vehicle,
-- src:18438 | it is taken to have an interest in any shares in which that scheme or vehicle has or is taken to have an interest.
@ref s 1279(3) interest through a scheme or vehicle (src:18435-18438)
GIVEN `the institution has an interest in a specified description of collective investment scheme (within the meaning of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), or in any other specified description of scheme or collective investment vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme or vehicle has or is taken to have an interest in the shares` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1279(3) the institution is taken to have an interest in the shares` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the institution has an interest in a specified description of collective investment scheme (within the meaning of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000), or in any other specified description of scheme or collective investment vehicle`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an institution has an interest— (a) in a specified description of collective investment scheme ..., or (b) in any other specified description of scheme or collective investment vehicle, it is taken to have an interest in any shares in which that scheme or vehicle has or is taken to have an interest" (a failed "where")
    ELSE `the scheme or vehicle has or is taken to have an interest in the shares`

-- src:18427 | (1) The shares to which section 1277 applies are shares—
-- src:18428 | (a) of a description traded on a specified market, and
-- src:18429 | (b) in which the institution has, or is taken to have, an interest.
@ref s 1279(1) shares to which section 1277 applies (src:18427-18429)
GIVEN `the shares are of a description traded on a specified market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the institution has, or is taken to have, an interest in the shares` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1279(1) the shares are shares to which section 1277 applies` MEANS
    IF `the shares are of a description traded on a specified market` AND `the institution has, or is taken to have, an interest in the shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The shares to which section 1277 applies are shares— (a) of a description traded on a specified market, and (b) in which the institution has, or is taken to have, an interest" (an "are" definition, not a "means" one: marginal reading M3)

-- ---- s 1280 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:18452 | (b) that in such a case it is sufficient, where that other person acts on behalf of more than one institution, that the reference is to information given in aggregated form, that is—
-- src:18453 | (i) relating to the exercise or non-exercise by that person of voting rights on behalf of more than one institution, or
-- src:18454 | (ii) relating to the instructions given by that person in respect of the exercise or non-exercise of voting rights on behalf of more than one institution, or
-- src:18455 | (iii) relating to the delegation by that person of functions in relation to the exercise or non-exercise of voting rights, or the giving of instructions in respect of the exercise or non-exercise of voting rights, on behalf of more than one institution.
@ref s 1280(5)(b) aggregated form (src:18452-18455)
GIVEN `the information relates to the exercise or non-exercise by that person of voting rights on behalf of more than one institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the instructions given by that person in respect of the exercise or non-exercise of voting rights on behalf of more than one institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the delegation by that person of functions in relation to the exercise or non-exercise of voting rights, or the giving of instructions in respect of the exercise or non-exercise of voting rights, on behalf of more than one institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1280(5)(b) the information is information given in aggregated form` MEANS
    IF       `the information relates to the exercise or non-exercise by that person of voting rights on behalf of more than one institution`
         OR  `the information relates to the instructions given by that person in respect of the exercise or non-exercise of voting rights on behalf of more than one institution`
         OR  `the information relates to the delegation by that person of functions in relation to the exercise or non-exercise of voting rights, or the giving of instructions in respect of the exercise or non-exercise of voting rights, on behalf of more than one institution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "information given in aggregated form, that is— (i) ..., or (ii) ..., or (iii) ..." (a "that is" definition, not a "means" one: marginal reading M3)

-- src:18456 | (6) References in this section to instructions are to instructions of any description, whether general or specific, whether binding or not and whether or not acted upon.
@ref s 1280(6) instructions (src:18456)
GIVEN `it is an instruction of any description, whether general or specific, whether binding or not and whether or not acted upon` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1280(6) the reference to instructions in section 1280 covers the instruction` MEANS
    IF `it is an instruction of any description, whether general or specific, whether binding or not and whether or not acted upon`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in this section to instructions are to instructions of any description"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1281: Disclosure of information under the Enterprise Act 2002 (the new section 241A of that Act)
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 1281 241A(2) kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 1281 241A(2)(a) information which comes to a public authority in connection with an investigation under Part 4, 5 or 6 of the 1973 Act or under section 11 of the Competition Act 1980`
    `s 1281 241A(2)(b) competition information within the meaning of section 351 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
    `s 1281 241A(2)(c) information which comes to a public authority in connection with an investigation under Part 3 or 4 or section 174 of the Enterprise Act 2002`
    `s 1281 241A(2)(d) information which comes to a public authority in connection with an investigation under the Competition Act 1998`
    `s 1281 241A(2) any other information`

-- src:18465 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to—
-- src:18466 | (a) information which comes to a public authority in connection with an investigation under Part 4, 5 or 6 of the 1973 Act or under section 11 of the Competition Act 1980;
-- src:18467 | (b) competition information within the meaning of section 351 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000;
-- src:18468 | (c) information which comes to a public authority in connection with an investigation under Part 3 or 4 or section 174 of this Act;
-- src:18469 | (d) information which comes to a public authority in connection with an investigation under the Competition Act 1998 (c. 41).
@ref s 1281 241A(2) information to which subsection (1) does not apply (src:18465-18469)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1281 241A(2) kind of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1281 241A(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1281 241A(2) any other information` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply to— (a) ... (d)": the list of excluded information is not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:18470 | (3) In subsection (1) “prescribed” means prescribed by order of the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1281 241A(3) "prescribed" (src:18470)
GIVEN `it is prescribed by order of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1281 241A(3) the information or proceedings are prescribed` MEANS
    IF `it is prescribed by order of the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In subsection (1) “prescribed” means prescribed by order of the Secretary of State"

DECLARE `s 1281 241A(1) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 1281 241A(1)(a) the purposes of, or in connection with, prescribed civil proceedings (including prospective proceedings) in the United Kingdom or elsewhere`
    `s 1281 241A(1)(b) the purposes of obtaining legal advice in relation to such proceedings`
    `s 1281 241A(1)(c) otherwise for the purposes of establishing, enforcing or defending legal rights that are or may be the subject of such proceedings`
    `s 1281 241A(1) any other purpose`

-- src:18461 | (1) A public authority which holds prescribed information to which section 237 applies may disclose that information to any person—
-- src:18462 | (a) for the purposes of, or in connection with, prescribed civil proceedings (including prospective proceedings) in the United Kingdom or elsewhere, or
-- src:18463 | (b) for the purposes of obtaining legal advice in relation to such proceedings, or
-- src:18464 | (c) otherwise for the purposes of establishing, enforcing or defending legal rights that are or may be the subject of such proceedings.
@ref s 1281 241A(1) disclosure by a public authority (src:18461-18464)
GIVEN `the authority is a public authority which holds prescribed information to which section 237 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 1281 241A(1) purpose`
      `subsection (1) does not apply to the information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1281 241A(1) the public authority may disclose the information to any person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (1) does not apply to the information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to—" the information described in (a) to (d)
        IF NOT (`the authority is a public authority which holds prescribed information to which section 237 applies`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public authority which holds prescribed information to which section 237 applies"
        IF purpose EQUALS `s 1281 241A(1) any other purpose`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may disclose that information to any person— (a) for the purposes of, or in connection with, prescribed civil proceedings ..., or (b) ..., or (c) ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:18474 | (c) must be made by statutory instrument subject to annulment in pursuance of a resolution of either House of Parliament.
@ref s 1281 241A(4)(c) procedure (src:18474)
GIVETH A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
`s 1281 241A(4)(c) the procedure for an order under section 241A` MEANS `s 1289 negative resolution procedure`

-- (5): a bar on the person to whom information is disclosed under section 241A.
-- src:18475 | (5) Information disclosed under this section must not be used by the person to whom it is disclosed for any purpose other than those specified in subsection (1)..
@ref s 1281 241A(5) use of the information disclosed (src:18475)
GIVEN `the information was disclosed under section 241A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person to whom it was disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is one specified in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1281 241A(5) the person is barred from using the information for the purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the information was disclosed under section 241A`)) OR (NOT (`the person is the person to whom it was disclosed`))
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information disclosed under this section must not be used by the person to whom it is disclosed"
        IF `the purpose is one specified in subsection (1)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any purpose other than those specified in subsection (1)": a purpose that is specified is outside the prohibition
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule: the person to whom the information is disclosed shall not use it for any
-- purpose other than those in subsection (1). The text gives no deadline and no consequence, so the rule has none.
DECLARE `s 1281 241A(5) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 1281 241A(5) the person to whom the information is disclosed`

DECLARE `s 1281 241A(5) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 1281 241A(5) uses the information for a purpose other than those specified in subsection (1)`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 1281 241A(5) party` `s 1281 241A(5) action`
`s 1281 241A(5) the recipient's prohibition on use` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1281 241A(5) the person to whom the information is disclosed`
    SHANT `s 1281 241A(5) uses the information for a purpose other than those specified in subsection (1)`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1282: Payment of expenses of winding up (the new section 176ZA of the Insolvency Act 1986, and Article 150ZA of
-- the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18481 | (2) In subsection (1)—
-- src:18482 | (a) the reference to assets of the company available for payment of general creditors does not include any amount made available under section 176A(2)(a);
@ref s 1282(1) 176ZA(2)(a) assets available for payment of general creditors (src:18481-18482)
GIVEN `the assets of the company that are available for payment of general creditors, before the exclusion below` IS A NUMBER
      `any amount made available under section 176A(2)(a)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1282(1) 176ZA(2)(a) the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors` MEANS
    max 0 (`the assets of the company that are available for payment of general creditors, before the exclusion below` MINUS `any amount made available under section 176A(2)(a)`)

-- src:18480 | (1) The expenses of winding up in England and Wales, so far as the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors are insufficient to meet them, have priority over any claims to property comprised in or subject to any floating charge created by the company and shall be paid out of any such property accordingly.
@ref s 1282(1) 176ZA(1) priority of the expenses of winding up (src:18480)
GIVEN `the winding up is in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors are insufficient to meet the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1282(1) 176ZA(1) the expenses of winding up have priority over claims to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the winding up is in England and Wales`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The expenses of winding up in England and Wales"
        IF `the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors are insufficient to meet the expenses`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so far as the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors are insufficient to meet them, have priority over any claims to property comprised in or subject to any floating charge" (the assets are sufficient)

-- "so far as the assets ... are insufficient": the part of the expenses that has the priority.
@ref s 1282(1) 176ZA(1) priority of the expenses of winding up (src:18480)
GIVEN `the expenses of winding up` IS A NUMBER
      `the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1282(1) 176ZA(1) the amount of the expenses that has priority over floating charge claims` MEANS
    max 0 (`the expenses of winding up` MINUS `the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors`)

DECLARE `s 1282 claimant` IS ONE OF
    `s 1282 176ZA(2)(b)(i) a holder of debentures secured by, or a holder of, the floating charge`
    `s 1282 176ZA(2)(b)(ii) a preferential creditor entitled to be paid out of that property in priority to them`
    `s 1282 another claimant`

-- src:18483 | (b) the reference to claims to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge is to the claims of—
-- src:18484 | (i) the holders of debentures secured by, or holders of, the floating charge, and
-- src:18485 | (ii) any preferential creditors entitled to be paid out of that property in priority to them.
@ref s 1282(1) 176ZA(2)(b) claims to floating charge property (src:18483-18485)
GIVEN claimant IS A `s 1282 claimant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1282(1) 176ZA(2)(b) the claim is a claim to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER claimant
    WHEN `s 1282 another claimant` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the reference to claims to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge is to the claims of— (i) ... and (ii) ..." (an "is to" statement with no "only": marginal reading M3)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:18489 | (4) References in this section to the expenses of the winding up are to all expenses properly incurred in the winding up, including the remuneration of the liquidator..
@ref s 1282(1) 176ZA(4) expenses of the winding up (src:18489)
GIVEN `it is an expense properly incurred in the winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1282(1) 176ZA(4) the expense is an expense of the winding up` MEANS
    IF `it is an expense properly incurred in the winding up`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- including the remuneration of the liquidator
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in this section to the expenses of the winding up are to all expenses properly incurred in the winding up, including the remuneration of the liquidator"

-- src:18493 | (2) In paragraph (1)—
-- src:18494 | (a) the reference to assets of the company available for payment of general creditors does not include any amount made available under Article 150A(2)(a);
@ref s 1282(2) 150ZA(2)(a) assets available for payment of general creditors (src:18493-18494)
GIVEN `the assets of the company that are available for payment of general creditors, before the exclusion below` IS A NUMBER
      `any amount made available under Article 150A(2)(a)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1282(2) 150ZA(2)(a) the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors` MEANS
    max 0 (`the assets of the company that are available for payment of general creditors, before the exclusion below` MINUS `any amount made available under Article 150A(2)(a)`)

-- src:18492 | (1) The expenses of winding up, so far as the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors are insufficient to meet them, have priority over any claims to property comprised in or subject to any floating charge created by the company and shall be paid out of any such property accordingly.
@ref s 1282(2) 150ZA(1) priority of the expenses of winding up (src:18492)
GIVEN `the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors are insufficient to meet the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1282(2) 150ZA(1) the expenses of winding up have priority over claims to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge` MEANS
    IF `the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors are insufficient to meet the expenses`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expenses of winding up, so far as the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors are insufficient to meet them, have priority over any claims to property comprised in or subject to any floating charge" (the assets are sufficient)

@ref s 1282(2) 150ZA(1) priority of the expenses of winding up (src:18492)
GIVEN `the expenses of winding up` IS A NUMBER
      `the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1282(2) 150ZA(1) the amount of the expenses that has priority over floating charge claims` MEANS
    max 0 (`the expenses of winding up` MINUS `the assets of the company available for payment of general creditors`)

-- src:18495 | (b) the reference to claims to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge is to the claims of—
-- src:18496 | (i) the holders of debentures secured by, or holders of, the floating charge, and
-- src:18497 | (ii) any preferential creditors entitled to be paid out of that property in priority to them.
@ref s 1282(2) 150ZA(2)(b) claims to floating charge property (src:18495-18497)
GIVEN claimant IS A `s 1282 claimant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1282(2) 150ZA(2)(b) the claim is a claim to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER claimant
    WHEN `s 1282 another claimant` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the reference to claims to property comprised in or subject to a floating charge is to the claims of— (i) ... and (ii) ..." (an "is to" statement with no "only": marginal reading M3)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:18501 | (4) References in this Article to the expenses of the winding up are to all expenses properly incurred in the winding up, including the remuneration of the liquidator..
@ref s 1282(2) 150ZA(4) expenses of the winding up (src:18501)
GIVEN `it is an expense properly incurred in the winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1282(2) 150ZA(4) the expense is an expense of the winding up` MEANS
    IF `it is an expense properly incurred in the winding up`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- including the remuneration of the liquidator
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in this Article to the expenses of the winding up are to all expenses properly incurred in the winding up, including the remuneration of the liquidator"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1283: Amendment of memorandum or articles of commonhold association
-- (the words substituted in paragraph 3(1) of Schedule 3 to the Commonhold and Leasehold Reform Act 2002)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18504 | In paragraph 3(1) of Schedule 3 to the Commonhold and Leasehold Reform Act 2002 (c. 15) (alteration of memorandum or articles by commonhold association to be of no effect until altered version registered with Land Registry) for “An alteration of the memorandum or articles of association” substitute “ Where a commonhold association alters its memorandum or articles at a time when the land specified in its memorandum is commonhold land, the alteration ”.
@ref s 1283 commonhold association (src:18504)
GIVEN `a commonhold association alters its memorandum or articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so at a time when the land specified in its memorandum is commonhold land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1283 paragraph 3(1) of Schedule 3 to the Commonhold and Leasehold Reform Act 2002 applies to the alteration` MEANS
    IF `a commonhold association alters its memorandum or articles` AND `it does so at a time when the land specified in its memorandum is commonhold land`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a commonhold association alters its memorandum or articles at a time when the land specified in its memorandum is commonhold land, the alteration" (a failed "where"; the effect of the paragraph, in the Act it amends, is not among the sources)
